course: dictionary
lesson: 8032
title: Refuel: fill up or eat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To refuel means to fill a car, plane, ship or other vehicle with fuel again. Cars refuel at petrol stations in the UK and at gas stations in the USA.
explain: Context helps you spot the second meaning. «After sport the body needs to refuel and repair; carbs and some protein, such as a sandwich, pasta, yoghurt or milk, help recovery.» The words sport, repair and recovery are clues: after sport your body needs food and drink, so refuel must mean to get your energy back.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence: «After sport the body needs to get its energy back and repair.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. In a joke, «Let's refuel» means «Let's have a snack.»
fact: Refuel means to fill up with fuel again.
fact: Informally, refuel means to eat and drink to get your energy back.
fact: In the UK people refuel cars with petrol; in the USA the word for petrol is gas.
fact: The spelling changes by country: refuelled (UK) and refueled (USA) both mean the same thing.
fact: A refuelling stop is a short break where a plane, car or person takes on fuel or food.
exercise: The car is almost empty, so the driver stops to refuel. What does refuel mean here? | Park it for the night | Wash the car | Lock all the doors | *Fill the car up with fuel again
exercise: «After sport the body needs to refuel and repair.» What does refuel mean here? | Stretch and warm up | *Eat and drink to get energy back | Sleep for a whole day | Put on a warm coat
exercise: Which food would help a body refuel after sport? | A bar of soap | A pencil case | A pair of trainers | *A yoghurt
test: A plane must refuel before it flies on. What does refuel mean? | *Fill up with fuel again | Take off very quickly | Fly very low | Land on the runway
test: Mum says, «Let's refuel,» and walks to the kitchen. What does she mean? | Let's go to bed | *Let's have a snack | Let's go shopping | Let's clean the kitchen
exam: In the USA drivers refuel at a gas station; in the UK, what do drivers buy there? | Bread | *Petrol | Pencils | Sweets
